  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The correct approach is to <b>duplicate the automated snapshot to create a manual snapshot and then share the manual snapshot</b> with the intended AWS account. Automated snapshots themselves cannot be shared directly due to AWS restrictions. You must first convert the automated snapshot into a manual one by copying it.<br/><br/>Let's review why the options are correct or incorrect:<br/><br/><b>First, duplicate the automated snapshot to generate a manual snapshot, and then share this new manual snapshot with the target AWS account.</b> - This is correct because AWS only permits sharing of manual DB snapshots across accounts. Automated snapshots must be copied to manual ones before they become shareable.<br/><br/><i>Choose the automated backup in the AWS Console and directly share it using the 'Share Snapshot' option.</i> - This is incorrect because automated snapshots lack the 'Share Snapshot' functionality; only manual snapshots can be shared.<br/><br/><i>Produce an encrypted manual snapshot from your RDS instance, and use either AWS Console or CLI to share it with another account.</i> - This answer is partially correct, but if the manual snapshot is encrypted and the encryption key is not shared or is AWS managed, you may face further restrictions. The core requirement is to make a manual snapshot first; encryption is an extra consideration.<br/><br/><i>It's not possible to share automated RDS snapshots with other AWS accounts.</i> - This is false: while automated snapshots themselves can't be shared, you can share them by creating a manual copy first.<br/><br/><b>Tip:</b> Always remember—AWS allows sharing of manual RDS snapshots, not automated ones, and encryption brings additional requirements regarding key sharing if enabled.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your team is developing a feature that uses an Amazon RDS MySQL instance to store email transaction data. Automated snapshots are enabled and functioning correctly. Recently, a business need emerged that requires the most recent snapshot to be shared with a different AWS account. <br/><br/>What steps should you follow to share this automated snapshot?</p>",
